      "writtenOn": "2022-07-15T13:27:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, so you tried using the fitness_fn(). I had a quick look at the patch and the only thing that stood out is that you created new rt_task_fits_capacity_and_may_preempt() but didn\u0027t replace all call site with the new function and had to add extra conditions of may_not_preempt unnecessarily instead.\n\nI think if you just create new rt_task_fits_cpu() that wrapps that 2 functions (with proper #ifdef CONFIG_..) and replace all call sites of rt_task_fits_capacity() with rt_task_fits_cpu() you should be okay.\n\nI can go and review Connon patch. But if you\u0027ll rework this, it might be easier to build on top of latest stuff.",
